{
  "audited_source_commit": "cda90d89ada0be4974655ccf746c78e3e61bc3bc",
  "units": "Bytes and milliseconds. Three independent sequential process runs per cell; reported values are medians.",
  "method": "Each bounded Node child initializes the pinned release WASM. Import open includes parsing and requested initial typing. Transform open includes import and grouping. Profile and proof are timed together after open. The difference between median open times estimates the extra cost of grouping and includes process variation. The app has no public group-in-place method. The extra cost for small samples can fall below noise.",
  "metrics": "Peak RSS uses the OS process high-water mark. Private resident and commit peaks are sampled at about 15 ms. WASM linear memory reports committed bytes. The Rust model reports estimated retained and temporary charges by stage. Freeing a dataset can leave linear allocator capacity available until the child or worker exits.",
  "repeat_procedure": "python -B benchmarks/data-revision.py GLUE WASM OUT [--revision] --repeats 3; each Node child has a 192 MiB V8 old-space cap, one synthetic table, at most 200000 rows, and a 60 s timeout.",
  "wasm_process_runs": {
